{{Repair Guide|Device=iPhone 8 Plus, iPhone 8|Difficulty=3. Hard|Affects parts=Main Logic Board, Front Camera, Charging Port Flex|Type=Soldering, Part Replacement}}

== Problem description ==
Device stuck on Apple logo loop. Boots sometimes but not stable. Charging is inconsistent – sometimes charges, sometimes doesn’t.
[[File:Iphone 8 series usb ic.png|thumb|Figure 1 - iPhone 8 / 8 Plus USB (Hydra) IC]]

== Symptoms ==

* Apple logo loop, device fails to boot reliably.
* Random charging behavior.
* New battery tested, no change.
* On DCPS: current draw jumps directly to 0.200A when prompting to boot.
* Not charging consistently even with known good cables.
* Hydra IC shows heating on thermal inspection.
[[File:Iphone 8 series front camera.png|thumb|Figure 2 - iPhone 8 / 8 Plus Front Camera]]

== Diagnostic Steps ==

# Visual Inspection
#* Check for corrosion or damage around Hydra IC, Tristar, and battery connector.
# DCPS Analysis
#* Normal preboot sequence should ramp (0.020A → 0.080A → 0.200A).
#* Direct jump to 0.200A suggests fault in Hydra/Tristar/PMIC path.
# Parts Swapping
#* Battery replaced → no effect.
#* Test with known good charging port flex.
#* Test with known good Front facing camera.
# Thermal Check
#* Hydra IC heating indicates abnormal activity.
[[File:8PlusChargePort.png|thumb|Figure 3 - iPhone 8 / 8 Plus Charge Port]]

== Repair Steps ==

# Replace/test charging port flex.
# Replace/test Front facing camera.
# If issue persists → replace Hydra IC.
# Test device boot and charging behavior on DCPS (expect proper ramping).
# Confirm final: stable boot, consistent charging, normal thermal profile.